{"id":"ec24beaa6ab5cdfe","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-prop-easton-products.md","title":"Easton Products","display":"prop-easton-products — Easton Products","type":"proposition","metadata":{"type":"proposition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-prop-easton-products","aliases":["58-prop-easton-products"],"display":"prop-easton-products — Easton Products","depends_on":["[[58-df-easton-product]]","[[../batch19/58-df-easton.md]]","[[../batch08/58-df-gch.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","[[../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md]]","[[../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"proposition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-prop-easton-products"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-prop-easton-products</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"prop-easton-products — Easton Products"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"beeacf2c76d5d297\" href=\"?note=beeacf2c76d5d297\" title=\"58-df-easton-product\">58-df-easton-product</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"08163b61fc3df1a5\" href=\"?note=08163b61fc3df1a5\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-easton.md\">../batch19/58-df-easton.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"f13d4bbe06c4eb5a\" href=\"?note=f13d4bbe06c4eb5a\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-gch.md\">../batch08/58-df-gch.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"2be08d4ee8aa1590\" href=\"?note=2be08d4ee8aa1590\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md\">../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"46b2495f214783c3\" href=\"?note=46b2495f214783c3\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md\">../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D,F,\\mathbb E_F,\\leq_E,\\vec P,\\vec\\leq,\\vec1\\in V\">\\(D,F,\\mathbb E_F,\\leq_E,\\vec P,\\vec\\leq,\\vec1\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Easton}_S(F,D)\">\\(\\mathrm{Easton}_S(F,D)\\)</span> is the set-sized Easton-function predicate</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{EastonProduct}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{EastonProduct}_S\\)</span> is the imported Easton-support product predicate</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|\\cdot|\">\\(|\\cdot|\\)</span> are the imported set-function and cardinality operators</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\\Vdash_{V,(\\mathbb E_F,\\leq_E)}\\varphi\">\\(p\\Vdash_{V,(\\mathbb E_F,\\leq_E)}\\varphi\\)</span> is the ambient forcing-relation class schema; forced formulas below are explicitly quoted</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{GCH}\">\\(\\mathrm{GCH}\\)</span> is the ground-model proposition used by this product presentation</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{prop\\text{-}easton\\text{-}products}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n&amp;\\mathrm{GCH}\n\\land\\mathrm{Easton}_S(F,D)\n\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in D\\;(\\kappa^+\\leq F(\\kappa))\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in D\\;\\Bigl(\n\\vec P(\\kappa)=\\{p\\in V:\\mathrm{Function}(p,\\operatorname{dom}(p),2)\n\\land\\operatorname{dom}(p)\\subseteq F(\\kappa)\\times\\kappa\n\\land|\\operatorname{dom}(p)|&lt;\\kappa\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{9em}\\land\\vec\\leq(\\kappa)=\n\\{\\langle p,q\\rangle\\in\\vec P(\\kappa)^2:p\\supseteq q\\}\n\\land\\vec1(\\kappa)=\\varnothing\\Bigr)\n\\land\\mathrm{EastonProduct}_S(\n\\mathbb E_F,\\leq_E,D,\\vec P,\\vec\\leq,\\vec1)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\n\\forall\\kappa\\in D\\;\\Bigl(\n\\vec1\\Vdash_{V,(\\mathbb E_F,\\leq_E)}\n\\ulcorner 2^{\\check\\kappa}=\\check{F(\\kappa)}\\urcorner\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{prop\\text{-}easton\\text{-}products}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n&amp;\\mathrm{GCH}\n\\land\\mathrm{Easton}_S(F,D)\n\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in D\\;(\\kappa^+\\leq F(\\kappa))\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in D\\;\\Bigl(\n\\vec P(\\kappa)=\\{p\\in V:\\mathrm{Function}(p,\\operatorname{dom}(p),2)\n\\land\\operatorname{dom}(p)\\subseteq F(\\kappa)\\times\\kappa\n\\land|\\operatorname{dom}(p)|&lt;\\kappa\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{9em}\\land\\vec\\leq(\\kappa)=\n\\{\\langle p,q\\rangle\\in\\vec P(\\kappa)^2:p\\supseteq q\\}\n\\land\\vec1(\\kappa)=\\varnothing\\Bigr)\n\\land\\mathrm{EastonProduct}_S(\n\\mathbb E_F,\\leq_E,D,\\vec P,\\vec\\leq,\\vec1)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\n\\forall\\kappa\\in D\\;\\Bigl(\n\\vec1\\Vdash_{V,(\\mathbb E_F,\\leq_E)}\n\\ulcorner 2^{\\check\\kappa}=\\check{F(\\kappa)}\\urcorner\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>An arbitrary product of Cohen forcings does not determine the continuum\nfunction.  The statement now records the Easton constraints, Easton\nsupport, coordinate forcings, and the ground-model hypothesis used by this\nstandard set-sized presentation.</li>\n<li>Each coordinate carrier, reverse-inclusion order, and top condition is fixed in the antecedent; the conclusion uses the actual product-top function <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\vec1\">\\(\\vec1\\)</span> and quotes each forcing-language instance.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-easton-product","status":"resolved","id":"beeacf2c76d5d297","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-easton-product]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch19/58-df-easton.md","status":"resolved","id":"08163b61fc3df1a5","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-df-easton.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch08/58-df-gch.md","status":"resolved","id":"f13d4bbe06c4eb5a","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-df-gch.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md","status":"resolved","id":"2be08d4ee8aa1590","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-cardinality.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md","status":"resolved","id":"46b2495f214783c3","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"D,F,\\mathbb E_F,\\leq_E,\\vec P,\\vec\\leq,\\vec1\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Easton}_S(F,D)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{EastonProduct}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"|\\cdot|","display":false},{"tex":"p\\Vdash_{V,(\\mathbb E_F,\\leq_E)}\\varphi","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{GCH}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{prop\\text{-}easton\\text{-}products}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}\n&\\mathrm{GCH}\n\\land\\mathrm{Easton}_S(F,D)\n\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in D\\;(\\kappa^+\\leq F(\\kappa))\\\\\n&{}\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in D\\;\\Bigl(\n\\vec P(\\kappa)=\\{p\\in V:\\mathrm{Function}(p,\\operatorname{dom}(p),2)\n\\land\\operatorname{dom}(p)\\subseteq F(\\kappa)\\times\\kappa\n\\land|\\operatorname{dom}(p)|<\\kappa\\}\\\\\n&\\hspace{9em}\\land\\vec\\leq(\\kappa)=\n\\{\\langle p,q\\rangle\\in\\vec P(\\kappa)^2:p\\supseteq q\\}\n\\land\\vec1(\\kappa)=\\varnothing\\Bigr)\n\\land\\mathrm{EastonProduct}_S(\n\\mathbb E_F,\\leq_E,D,\\vec P,\\vec\\leq,\\vec1)\\\\\n&\\quad\\to\n\\forall\\kappa\\in D\\;\\Bigl(\n\\vec1\\Vdash_{V,(\\mathbb E_F,\\leq_E)}\n\\ulcorner 2^{\\check\\kappa}=\\check{F(\\kappa)}\\urcorner\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\vec1","display":false}],"bytes":2237,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-3952","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-prop-easton-products.md|58-prop-easton-products]]（batch18）"}],"outgoing":["beeacf2c76d5d297","08163b61fc3df1a5","f13d4bbe06c4eb5a","36d7463d215be751","2be08d4ee8aa1590","46b2495f214783c3"]}